# Written in full by customize.sh at install time.
#
# Nothing is hardcoded here: the gadget HAL's domain and the root manager's domain are read from
# the device during installation, and only rules whose source is a restricted domain are written -
# the root domain is unrestricted, so rules from it would be dead weight.
#
# If either domain cannot be determined, the installer aborts instead of falling back to a name
# from another device. A device whose installer did not rewrite this file has no IRA policy, and
# the HAL hook is denied: this is a placeholder, not a fallback.
